  "verbalization": "sec-Butyl acetate, (-)- is linked to SNB-78 through a series of molecular targets that are all ultimately directed toward SNB-78. The evidence suggests that sec-Butyl acetate, (-)- acts as a target for multiple compounds, including SNU-387, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which are all known to target SNB-78. This implies that sec-Butyl acetate, (-)- may exert its biological effects through a mechanism that involves these compounds, potentially through shared pathways or interactions. The integration of these targets highlights a possible role for sec-Butyl acetate, (-)- in modulating SNB-78 activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a network of interactions where sec-Butyl acetate, (-)- serves as a starting point for a series of molecular targets that ultimately influence SNB-78.",
